      "inputs": [],
      "outputs": [],
      "properties": {
        "ue_properties": {
          "widget_ue_connectable": {},
          "version": "7.8",
          "input_ue_unconnectable": {}
        }
      },
      "widgets_values": [
        "## Prompt weighting (KJNodes: MOSS-Image Prompt Weight)\n\nWrite `(phrase:weight)` anywhere in the positive prompt:\n\n- `(phrase:-1)` removes a concept, `(phrase:0.5)` tones it down — the reliable direction\n- `(phrase:1.5)` / `(phrase:2)` emphasize it — visible at 2, subtle at 1.5\n- `strength` scales every weight at once (0 = off, 1 = as written)\n\nComfyUI's usual `(word:1.2)` does nothing on MOSS-Image: the Qwen3.5 encoder reads the brackets as text. This node strips them, encodes the clean prompt and weights the phrase inside every attention block. Both outputs (model + conditioning) go to the guider. A phrase can't contain `(`, `)` or `:`.\n\nMOSS-Image likes long, descriptive prompts; put exact text to render in quotes."
      ],
      "widgets_values_named": {
        "text": "## Prompt weighting (KJNodes: MOSS-Image Prompt Weight)\n\nWrite `(phrase:weight)` anywhere in the positive prompt:\n\n- `(phrase:-1)` removes a concept, `(phrase:0.5)` tones it down — the reliable direction\n- `(phrase:1.5)` / `(phrase:2)` emphasize it — visible at 2, subtle at 1.5\n- `strength` scales every weight at once (0 = off, 1 = as written)\n\nComfyUI's usual `(word:1.2)` does nothing on MOSS-Image: the Qwen3.5 encoder reads the brackets as text. This node strips them, encodes the clean prompt and weights the phrase inside every attention block. Both outputs (model + conditioning) go to the guider. A phrase can't contain `(`, `)` or `:`.\n\nMOSS-Image likes long, descriptive prompts; put exact text to render in quotes."
      },
      "color": "#432",
      "bgcolor": "#653"
    },
